Java Vector

Vector is a dynamic array in Java that grows automatically when elements are added. It is similar to ArrayList, but Vector is synchronized (thread-safe).

Import
import java.util.Vector;
Create a Vector
import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Vector<String> v = new Vector<>();

        v.add("Java");
        v.add("Python");
        v.add("C++");

        System.out.println(v);
    }
}
